.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt DH_NEW_BY_NID 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm DH_new_by_nid ,
.Nm DH_get_nid
.Nd create or get DH named parameters
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/dh.h
The following functions have been deprecated since OpenSSL 3.0, and can
be hidden entirely by defining
.Ar OPENSSL_API_COMPAT
with a suitable version value, see
.Xr openssl_user_macros 7 :
.Ft DH *
.Fo DH_new_by_nid
.Fa "int nid"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo DH_get_nid
.Fa "const DH *dh"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn DH_new_by_nid
creates and returns a DH structure containing named parameters
.Fa nid .
Currently
.Fa nid
must be
.Sy NID_ffdhe2048 ,
.Sy NID_ffdhe3072 ,
.Sy NID_ffdhe4096 ,
.Sy NID_ffdhe6144 ,
.Sy NID_ffdhe8192 ,
.Sy NID_modp_1536 ,
.Sy NID_modp_2048 ,
.Sy NID_modp_3072 ,
.Sy NID_modp_4096 ,
.Sy NID_modp_6144
or
.Sy NID_modp_8192 .
.Pp
.Fn DH_get_nid
determines if the parameters contained in
.Fa dh
match any named safe prime group.
It returns the NID corresponding to the matching parameters or
.Sy NID_undef
if there is no match.
This function is deprecated.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn DH_new_by_nid
returns a set of DH parameters or
.Dv NULL
if an error occurred.
.Pp
.Fn DH_get_nid
returns the NID of the matching set of parameters for p and g and
optionally q, otherwise it returns
.Sy NID_undef
if there is no match.
.Sh HISTORY
All of these functions were deprecated in OpenSSL 3.0.
